<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ScariaIncubation.xml             UtinniPatches - SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2 build pass

  scarlands_kit_spec.md §3 (plated-grazer scaria onset). Pure XML per the
  spec's own route: vanilla wildAnimalScariaChance already rolls vanilla
  Scaria onto some wild animals at spawn, but Hediff_Scaria.TickInterval
  only auto-starts the rage for humanlikes and FACTIONED animals (decompile-
  confirmed, quoted in the kit spec) — a wild scaria animal otherwise stays
  calm forever. This hediff is the fuse: once armed (RUT_ScariaOnsetArming.xml,
  GameConditionDefs/), it climbs on its own and its own final stage forces
  the manhunter flip vanilla scaria never would on a wild animal.

  severityPerDayRange (0.1~0.25), left as severityPerDay=0 plus the range:
  HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay.CalculateSeverityPerDay (decompile-
  confirmed) rolls ONE rate per pawn at CompPostPostAdd and keeps it for the
  hediff's life — exactly the spec's own "severity 0.1–0.25/day, randomized
  per pawn," with zero new C#. maxSeverity 1.0 makes the spec's own invented
  "incubation 4-12 days" arithmetic transparent: 1.0/0.25 = 4 days fastest,
  1.0/0.1 = 10 days slowest (the spec's own "4-12" is itself an
  approximation — this build pass did not stretch the range to hit 12
  exactly, since the rate figures are the spec's real INVENTED numbers and
  the day-count was only ever their derived illustration).

  Final stage's mentalStateGivers -> ManhunterPermanent, mtbDays 0.5: the
  spec's own INVENTED figure, verbatim ("final-stage giver MTB 0.5 days").
  Once that mental state fires, the ANIMAL'S OWN vanilla Scaria hediff
  (already present — this condition only arms pawns carrying it, see
  RUT_ScariaOnsetArming.xml's requiredHediff) takes over via its own 5-day
  (300000-tick) death clock — nothing else to wire here, per the spec's own
  "we add the fuse, vanilla burns it."

  No MayRequire: HediffWithComps and HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay are
  both vanilla.
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RUT_ScariaIncubation</defName>
    <label>scaria incubation</label>
    <description>The madness is coming. Nothing shows yet — no sores, no change in temper — but somewhere under the plating it has already started, and it will not stop.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.5,0.1,0.1)</defaultLabelColor>
    <minSeverity>0.0001</minSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>0.0001</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>incubating</label>
        <becomeVisible>false</becomeVisible>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>1.0</minSeverity>
        <label>on the verge</label>
        <mentalStateGivers>
          <li>
            <mentalState>ManhunterPermanent</mentalState>
            <mtbDays>0.5</mtbDays>
          </li>
        </mentalStateGivers>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>0</severityPerDay>
        <severityPerDayRange>0.1~0.25</severityPerDayRange>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
